# Copy to .env.local for the local preview, and set the same names in the
# Vercel project environment for the deployed build. Never commit .env.local.
#
# Both are OPTIONAL. With neither set the app still runs: it stores the
# watchlist in the browser, and reads a title and a channel from oEmbed.

# YouTube Data API v3. Without it the app falls back to oEmbed, which gives
# a title and a channel but no duration and no upload date.
#
# Leave this key UNRESTRICTED by HTTP referrer. It is used server-side, and a
# server sends no referrer, so a browser-restricted key is refused outright
# with "Requests from referer <empty> are blocked".
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

# Google Drive sync. This is a PUBLIC identifier: it reaches the browser, and
# /api/config hands it over on request. It lives here so the repository
# carries no credentials, not because it is secret.
#
# What actually protects it is in the Google Cloud console. Add your deployed
# origin and http://localhost:3000 to the OAuth client's Authorized
# JavaScript origins.
#
# The OAuth client SECRET is deliberately absent. The browser-only token flow
# never uses one, so there is no secret for this project to leak.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
